this woman named Dee Dee Moore. Dee Dee Moore was a certified nurse's assistant who ran a nursing staffing agency called American Medical Professionals. In 2008, she attended a small business conference in Florida where she observed a panel discussion featuring a real estate agent. The agent spoke of having once sold a house to a lottery winner named Abraham Shakespeare. He had changed the way she viewed wealth, specifically that money does not equal happiness. After hearing Abraham's story, Dee Dee Moore was inspired to write about him for a magazine article. In October 2008, she arranged to meet Abraham.
