This meant anyone who wanted funds would have to go through duty. Abraham had been moving his money from bank to bank on a whim. Dee Dee advised him to secure his leftover money in a single Bank of America account under his own name. Dee Dee, Abraham and Judy got together periodically to discuss Abraham's finances with Dee Dee keeping record of the meetings for the bank. She was dismayed to learn that Abraham was using his money for what she had noted as criminal activity. He was removed as an authorized signer of his account, leaving just Dee Dee and Judy with access. They became a buffer between Abraham and any unwise financial decisions. Dee Dee also helped to manage all of Abraham's assets, including his property.
这意味着任何想要资金的人都必须通过朱迪。亚伯拉罕一直随心所欲地在银行之间转移他的钱。迪迪建议他将剩余的钱存入他自己名下的一个美国银行账户中。迪迪、亚伯拉罕和朱迪定期聚在一起讨论亚伯拉罕的财务状况，迪迪为银行记录了会议内容。她沮丧地发现亚伯拉罕正在将他的钱用于她所记录的犯罪活动。他被取消了账户授权签字人的资格，只剩下迪迪和朱迪有权访问。他们成为了亚伯拉罕和任何不明智财务决策之间的缓冲。迪迪还帮助管理亚伯拉罕的所有资产，包括他的房产。

39
00:34:55.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Dee Dee encouraged Abraham to start living his life. In their recorded interview, she asked where he would like to go. He responded, It don't matter to me, I'm not a picky person. Dee Dee offered suggestions, California, a foreign country. Seemingly irritated by Dee Dee's prying, Abraham motioned for her to turn off the camera. Are you gonna miss your home, Dee Dee asked. Abraham responded,
迪迪鼓励亚伯拉罕开始过自己的生活。在他们录制的采访中，她问他想去哪里。他回答说：“对我来说无所谓，我不是一个挑剔的人。”迪迪提出了建议，加利福尼亚，一个外国。亚伯拉罕似乎对迪迪的打探感到恼火，示意她关掉摄像机。“你会想念你的家吗？”迪迪问。亚伯拉罕回答说：

40
