00:36:18.000 --> 00:37:16.000
Having grown attached to Abraham and his plight, she agreed. When Abraham left Lakeland, Dee Dee spread conflicting rumors about where he'd gone and why to prevent him from being traced. She also shared alleged sightings of Abraham so people knew he was alright. He had left Dee Dee his cell phone, allowing her to send texts on his behalf to his friends and family. Whenever concerns for Abraham grew, Dee Dee used money he had given her to pay people to claim they'd heard from him. She paid Greg Smith $300 to call Detective David Wallace and report a false sighting of Abraham in Miami. She gave Greg a further $350 to call Abraham's mother. She'd even broken attorney-client privilege by staging a call to Abraham's attorney in October.
由于对亚伯拉罕和他的困境产生了感情，她同意了。当亚伯拉罕离开莱克兰时，迪迪散布了关于他去了哪里以及原因的相互矛盾的谣言，以防止他被追踪。她还分享了所谓的亚伯拉罕的目击消息，让人们知道他很好。他把手机留给了迪迪，让她可以代表他给朋友和家人发短信。每当人们对亚伯拉罕的担忧增加时，迪迪就用他给她的钱付钱给别人，让他们声称收到过他的消息。她付给格雷格·史密斯300美元，让他给大卫·华莱士侦探打电话，报告在迈阿密看到亚伯拉罕的虚假消息。她又给了格雷格350美元，让他给亚伯拉罕的母亲打电话。她甚至在10月份通过安排给亚伯拉罕的律师打电话，打破了律师与客户的特权。

42
00:37:16.000 --> 00:38:14.000
Abraham had told her, you handle all the business, I got to go. When approached by detectives, Dee Dee became emotional as she divulged what she'd done. She claimed not to know where Abraham was, but maintained that the two had met up and spoken since he fell off the grid in April 2009. Dee Dee said she'd initially been under the impression that she was simply keeping things in order until Abraham came home. But over time, she suspected he never intended to return. She felt she had misjudged him, saying, I've got all this trouble on me when all I was trying to do is help the man. Dee Dee willingly assisted investigators with their inquiries. Eventually, she admitted there were several other reasons Abraham might have fled.
