50
00:43:45.000 --> 00:44:37.000
She made up a story that someone had recognized Abraham and he'd had to pay a police officer $20,000 to keep his secret. In reference to herself, Dee Dee wrote, Don't worry about Dee, if she goes to jail she will be okay, the charges won't stick. There are too many people that know why I left, I gave her enough money, she knew what to expect. She should have not gotten involved, so now she just has to deal with it. Remembering that Abraham was illiterate and incapable of writing long-winded prose, Dee Dee added, I still can't write a letter, a good friend is typing it for me. I will see you, I promise, just give me some time.
她编造了一个故事，说有人认出了亚伯拉罕，他不得不付给一名警察2万美元来保守秘密。在提到自己时，迪迪写道：“别担心迪，如果她坐牢，她会没事的，指控不会成立。有太多人知道我为什么离开，我给了她足够的钱，她知道会发生什么。她本不该卷入其中，所以现在她只能自己处理了。”想到亚伯拉罕目不识丁，写不出长篇大论，迪迪补充道：“我还是不会写信，是一个好朋友在帮我打字。我会见你的，我保证，只是给我一点时间。”

51
00:44:37.000 --> 00:45:38.000
Greg Smith was impressed, the letter didn't sound like it had come from Dee Dee at all. They printed it off and slid it into an envelope. The pair wiped the room down with towels, then they drove to Abraham's mother's home where Greg placed the letter in her mailbox. But any hopes that the letter would help Dee Dee were dashed when it failed to make the news? Elizabeth didn't speak about it publicly and the police seemed unaware of its existence. Instead, investigators upped the reward for information to $10,000 with the promise that any tipsters wouldn't have to testify in future court proceedings. The county sheriff announced, None of the circumstances and none of the investigation we've completed up to this point leads us to believe Abraham Shakespeare is still alive.
格雷格·史密斯印象深刻，这封信听起来一点也不像出自迪迪之手。他们打印出来并塞进信封。两人用毛巾擦拭了房间，然后开车去亚伯拉罕母亲家，格雷格把信放进了她的邮箱。但任何希望这封信能帮助迪迪的想法都在它未能登上新闻后破灭了。伊丽莎白没有公开谈论它，警察似乎也不知道它的存在。相反，调查人员将悬赏金提高到1万美元，并承诺举报人将来不必在法庭诉讼中作证。县治安官宣布：“到目前为止，我们完成的所有调查情况都没有让我们相信亚伯拉罕·莎士比亚还活着。”

52
